commit: e3b16527cc0336de947c69d776576faf00dd816d

Task 04 of ticket 10 moves the note counter's rule out of the app and into `AnkyDomain`, so unit tests reach it. Four
UI tests checked that rule on a simulator, and they are gone now.

### The problem

The counter's rule sat in `NoteSection`, in `App/NewEntry`. It hid the counter at 40 or more characters left, counted
down below that, and said "Limit reached" at 240. No unit test could reach that code, so four UI tests were the only
check. Each one took a simulator and a few seconds.

### How it is solved

- `AnkyDomain` has `NoteCounter`, with `left(Int)` and `limitReached`, and `EntryDraft.noteCounter`. The property is
  `nil` while 40 or more characters are left. It returns a value, not words, so the next task can map it to catalog
  entries with plural forms.
- `NoteSection` maps that value to the same words as before: "N left" and "Limit reached". Nothing on screen changes.
- A note counts each accented letter and each emoji once, as the field does. The unit tests cover both.
- A note of only spaces already counts as a change, because `EntryDraft` compares notes exactly. A unit test now pins
  that, so the swipe block it supports has a unit test too.

### Deleted UI tests and the unit tests that replace them

| Deleted UI test | Unit test that replaces it |
|---|---|
| `NoteTests/testCounterReadsTenLeft` | `NoteCounterTests/noteCounterReadsTenLeftAtTwoHundredThirtyCharacters` |
| `NoteTests/testCounterReadsOneLeft` | `NoteCounterTests/noteCounterReadsOneLeftAtTwoHundredThirtyNineCharacters` |
| `NoteTests/testNoteCounterIsHiddenForAShortNote` | `NoteCounterTests/noteCounterIsNilWithNoNote` and `NoteCounterTests/noteCounterIsNilAtFortyCharactersLeft` |
| `CancelTests/testSwipeDownIsBlockedAfterNoteOfOnlySpaces` | `NoteCounterTests/noteOfOnlySpacesIsAChangeToTheDraftItOpenedFrom` |

`NoteTests/testNoteStopsAtTheLimit` stays as the one note-limit journey on screen. It now types 230 characters first and
checks "10 left", then types the rest and checks "Limit reached". So both wordings still reach the screen once.

### Manual verification

- The full UI suite ran on a local simulator in light: 37 of 38 tests passed. `NoFutureTimeTests/testPickerStopsAtNow`
  failed on both iterations before 23:00 local time. It fails the same way on the base commit, so this change did not
  cause it. It is a date picker test, and this change does not touch the picker.

